  "description": "OFABUU crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H175 O47 P6 Tb8 2-,2(C3 H10 N1 1+). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb6 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb7 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb8 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.649-3.929 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.46-111.28°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (NH3iPr)2[Tb8(O3PtBu)6(μ3-OH)2(O2CtBu)12(H2O)(HOiBu)]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
